---

<Base title="CISNET · Case Study · Pravine Mani" description="Migrated a Toronto IT certification training company off legacy PHP onto Next.js 16. 200+ pSEO pages. Custom admin portal. Lead pipeline. 3 months. Solo." footerVariant="case-study" jsonLd={jsonLd}>


<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/work/" style="color: var(--text-dim);">work</a>
    <span style="color: var(--text-muted, #444);">/</span>
    <a href="/work/" style="color: var(--text-dim);">case studies</a>
    <span style="color: var(--text-muted, #444);">/</span>
    <span class="you">cisnet</span>
  </div>
  <h1>CISNET: IT certification training.<br><span class="accent" style="color: #dc2626; -webkit-text-fill-color: #dc2626;">Marketing site + SEO rebuild.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">Migrated a Toronto IT certification training company off legacy PHP onto Next.js 16. Full programmatic SEO, a lead pipeline, and an admin portal, in three months, solo. Ranking authority preserved through a 70+ URL redirect map.</p>

  <div class="cs-hero-meta">
    <div class="cell"><div class="k">CLIENT</div><div class="v">IT Training · Toronto</div></div>
    <div class="cell"><div class="k">SCOPE</div><div class="v"><span class="bl">Site + SEO + Pipeline + Admin Portal</span></div></div>
    <div class="cell"><div class="k">DELIVERED</div><div class="v">2025-Q4 · 3 MO</div></div>
    <div class="cell"><div class="k">ROLE</div><div class="v">Solo · End-to-end</div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">

  <!-- Problem -->
  <div class="cs-section reveal">
    <div class="lab-col"><span class="num">01 / 05</span><span>THE PROBLEM</span></div>
    <div class="body-col">
      <h2>Legacy PHP that couldn't grow.</h2>
      <p>CISNET's existing site was a hand-coded PHP build from 2014. It was maintainable because one person knew where everything lived, and brittle because <strong>nobody else could ship into it without an outage</strong>. Marketing wanted new certification pages, paid campaigns into specific cohorts, and leads captured into a CRM. In practice, every new page was a Friday deploy with the lights flickering.</p>
      <p>The deeper issue was SEO momentum. The legacy site ranked for ~70 cert-related queries, and any redesign that didn't preserve those URLs risked tanking organic traffic for a quarter or more. The business drew ~40% of its intake from that organic flow.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Brittle stack:</strong> PHP 5.6, no test suite, manual FTP deploys</li>
        <li><strong>No lead infrastructure:</strong> contact-form-to-email only, no CRM, no admin view</li>
        <li><strong>SEO at risk:</strong> 70+ ranked legacy URLs that couldn't break</li>
        <li><strong>Marketing blocked:</strong> couldn't ship landing pages without engineering</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Approach -->
  <div class="cs-section reveal">
    <div class="lab-col"><span class="num">02 / 05</span><span>THE APPROACH</span></div>
    <div class="body-col">
      <h2>Next.js 16 + programmatic SEO + lead infrastructure.</h2>
      <p>Three parallel workstreams over 12 weeks. <strong>Stream 1 (weeks 1-4)</strong> stood up the Next.js 16, Supabase, and Vercel foundation, ported the marketing pages 1:1, and ran the redirect map in dev. <strong>Stream 2 (weeks 4-8)</strong> handled programmatic SEO: 200+ cert × city pages generated from a structured content model, plus sitemap.xml and 7 distinct schema types. <strong>Stream 3 (weeks 8-12)</strong> built the lead pipeline: a Facebook Lead Ads webhook with HMAC verification, Supabase storage, the admin portal, Resend transactional email, and Stripe Checkout for paid courses.</p>
      <p>The hardest early call was <strong>how aggressive to be on the redirect strategy.</strong> I mapped every legacy URL individually rather than rely on Next.js catch-all rewrites. It was slower to build, and Google indexed the new URLs with full link equity inside 6 weeks instead of 6 months.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Foundation:</strong> Next.js 16 (app router), TypeScript strict, Supabase, Vercel</li>
        <li><strong>SEO surface:</strong> 200+ pSEO pages generated from a cert × city matrix</li>
        <li><strong>Redirects:</strong> 70+ legacy URLs mapped individually (not catch-all)</li>
        <li><strong>Schema:</strong> 7 types: Course, LocalBusiness, FAQPage, Organization, BreadcrumbList, ContactPoint, WebSite</li>
        <li><strong>Lead pipeline:</strong> FB Lead Ads → HMAC-verified webhook → Supabase → admin portal → Resend</li>
        <li><strong>Payments:</strong> Stripe Checkout + course-enrollment webhook</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Stack -->
  <div class="cs-section reveal">
    <div class="lab-col"><span class="num">03 / 05</span><span>THE STACK</span></div>
    <div class="body-col">
      <h2>Boring, fast, debuggable.</h2>
      <p>The default opinionated stack: Next.js, Supabase, Vercel. A CMS for the marketing pages was an option, but the editorial volume didn't warrant the operational tax. Page content lives in MDX in the repo, and engineers ship copy through PRs.</p>
      <div class="stack-flat">
        <span class="chip daily">Next.js 16</span>
        <span class="chip daily">TypeScript</span>
        <span class="chip daily">Vercel</span>
        <span class="chip">Supabase</span>
        <span class="chip">Tailwind</span>
        <span class="chip">Stripe</span>
        <span class="chip">Resend</span>
        <span class="chip">FB Lead Ads API</span>
        <span class="chip">MDX</span>
        <span class="chip">Zod</span>
        <span class="chip">React Hook Form</span>
        <span class="chip">Plausible</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Timeline -->
  <div class="cs-section reveal">
    <div class="lab-col"><span class="num">04 / 05</span><span>THE TIMELINE</span></div>
    <div class="body-col">
      <h2>12 weeks. 3 streams. No scope creep.</h2>
      <p>Scope locked in week 0. Anything that came up afterward went onto a "v2 list," and none of it shipped during the engagement.</p>
      <div class="timeline-rail">
        <div class="step"><span class="when">WK 0</span><span class="what"><strong>Kickoff + scope lock.</strong> Written spec signed. Redirect map drafted from server logs.</span></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="when">WK 1–4</span><span class="what"><strong>Foundation stream.</strong> Next.js 16 scaffold, marketing pages 1:1 port, Supabase schema, Vercel deploys, redirect map in dev.</span></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="when">WK 4–8</span><span class="what"><strong>SEO stream.</strong> Cert × city content model, 200+ pSEO page generation, 7 schema types, sitemap.xml + robots.txt, internal-link graph.</span></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="when">WK 8–12</span><span class="what"><strong>Pipeline stream.</strong> FB Lead Ads webhook + HMAC verification, admin portal, Resend transactional email, Stripe checkout, payment webhooks.</span></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="when">WK 12</span><span class="what"><strong>Cutover + monitoring.</strong> Production deploy, DNS swap, redirect map active, Plausible + Search Console + Sentry wired up. 14-day support window.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Impact -->
  <div class="cs-section reveal">
    <div class="lab-col"><span class="num">05 / 05</span><span>THE IMPACT</span></div>
    <div class="body-col">
      <h2>What it enabled.</h2>
      <p>Headline numbers from the engagement, technical surface only. Business KPIs are CISNET's to disclose.</p>
      <div class="impact-grid">
        <div class="impact-card"><div class="k">PSEO PAGES</div><div class="v">200+</div><div class="desc">Cert × city programmatic pages. Indexed within 6 weeks of cutover.</div></div>
        <div class="impact-card"><div class="k">LEGACY URLS PRESERVED</div><div class="v">70+</div><div class="desc">Individually-mapped redirects. Ranking authority preserved on every URL.</div></div>
        <div class="impact-card"><div class="k">SCHEMA TYPES</div><div class="v">7</div><div class="desc">Course, LocalBusiness, FAQPage, Organization, BreadcrumbList, ContactPoint, WebSite.</div></div>
        <div class="impact-card"><div class="k">LIGHTHOUSE PERF</div><div class="v">98+</div><div class="desc">Production performance score across every marketing route.</div></div>
        <div class="impact-card"><div class="k">ADMIN PORTAL</div><div class="v">FULL</div><div class="desc">Custom portal for leads, enrollments, content, payments. Built from scratch on Next.js + Supabase.</div></div>
        <div class="impact-card"><div class="k">DELIVERED IN</div><div class="v">3 MO</div><div class="desc">Fixed-price. Fixed-scope. Zero scope creep across 3 streams.</div></div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 20px;">Beyond the numbers: marketing ships new certification pages through MDX without engineering. Lead routing is observable end to end. Ad campaigns now target specific cohort × city combinations that previously had no landing page.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 44px;">The admin portal I built.</h2>
      <p>The contact-form-to-email setup became a full operations console: lead pipeline, students, enrollments, email campaigns, content, and analytics, built from scratch on Next.js 16 + Supabase. No off-the-shelf CRM, no third-party analytics tax. The team runs the business from here.</p>
      <div class="cs-shots">
        <figure>
          <img src="/case-studies/cisnet/admin-dashboard.webp" alt="CISNET admin portal dashboard: new leads, pipeline, enrollments and revenue KPI cards above a recent-leads list" width="1400" height="739" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption><span class="t">Pipeline at a glance</span> Leads, enrollments and revenue KPIs with the latest leads inline. Customer details blurred for this case study.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/case-studies/cisnet/admin-analytics.webp" alt="CISNET admin portal traffic-sources analytics: channel distribution donut with page-views and leads broken down by channel" width="1400" height="871" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption><span class="t">First-party analytics</span> Channel attribution for page views and leads, from my own event pipeline, no third-party analytics dependency.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/case-studies/cisnet/admin-seo.webp" alt="CISNET admin portal SEO overview: live Google Search Console clicks, impressions, top queries and top pages" width="1400" height="749" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption><span class="t">Search Console, in-app</span> Live GSC clicks, impressions, top queries and pages via a service-account API integration I built in.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 44px;">Search results I drove.</h2>
      <p>After taking over the SEO operation in late April 2026, I rebuilt the content architecture and structured data, fixed the technical foundation (canonicals, redirects, Core Web Vitals), and shipped a free tools and study-resource layer (subnet calculator, practice quizzes, cheat sheets). Measured in Google Search Console across 28-day windows ending April 30 against June 18, 2026:</p>
      <div class="impact-grid">
        <div class="impact-card"><div class="k">Search impressions</div><div class="v">3×</div><div class="desc">7,600 to 22,500 per 28 days. Monthly impressions up 108% from April to May.</div></div>
        <div class="impact-card"><div class="k">Ranking pages</div><div class="v">5.4×</div><div class="desc">27 to 145 distinct pages earning search impressions.</div></div>
        <div class="impact-card"><div class="k">Query footprint</div><div class="v">855 → 1,000+</div><div class="desc">Distinct queries the site surfaces for (GSC reporting cap reached).</div></div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 14px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-dim);">Source: Google Search Console, sc-domain property, queried live via a service-account API integration I built into the admin portal. Clicks up ~19% over the same window and compounding as the larger footprint matures; off-page authority is the next lever.</p>

      <div class="cs-proof">
        <figure>
          <img src="/case-studies/cisnet/gsc-growth-16mo.webp" alt="Google Search Console 16-month performance for cisnet.ca: 1.66K clicks and 104K impressions, trending upward" width="1400" height="973" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption><span class="t">16-month trajectory</span> 1.66K clicks · 104K impressions, accelerating in recent months.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/case-studies/cisnet/gsc-pages-indexed.webp" alt="Google Search Console page indexing for cisnet.ca: 145 pages indexed, the indexed count rising over time" width="1400" height="973" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption><span class="t">Indexed footprint</span> 27 → 145 indexed pages as the new architecture matured.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/case-studies/cisnet/gsc-top-queries.webp" alt="Google Search Console top queries for cisnet.ca, ranking for commercial CCNA terms beyond the brand name" width="1400" height="973" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption><span class="t">Query footprint</span> Ranking well beyond the brand into commercial CCNA terms.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/case-studies/cisnet/gsc-traffic-trend.webp" alt="Google Search Console 3-month performance trend for cisnet.ca, clicks and impressions both rising" width="1400" height="973" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption><span class="t">Recent trend</span> Latest 3-month window, clicks and impressions both climbing.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-dim);">Live Google Search Console dashboards. Account identity blurred; all metrics unedited.</p>

      <div class="cs-pullquote">
        <blockquote>Async-first actually works the way he runs it. Daily Looms, written summaries, no meeting tax. The migration ran 3 months without a single live call drift.</blockquote>
        <div class="pq-src"><div class="pq-av">MP</div><div class="pq-meta"><span class="pq-name">Mani P</span><span class="pq-role">Ops Lead · CISNET</span></div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="confidential">
        <strong>Note:</strong> Search performance above is from Google Search Console. Downstream business KPIs (lead-to-enrollment rates, MRR impact) are the client's to disclose and aren't shown here.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <div class="final-cta reveal" style="text-align: center;">
    <p style="margin: 0;">Similar surface area: a legacy stack to migrate, SEO to preserve, lead infrastructure to build. <a href="/contact/" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);">Discuss the project →</a></p>
  </div>

</section>




</Base>
<style is:global>
.reveal { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(16px); transition: all 600ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1); }
.reveal.visible { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }

.cs-hero-meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--border); border: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
.cs-hero-meta .cell { background: var(--bg-card); padding: 16px 20px; }
.cs-hero-meta .cell .k { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--text-dim); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 5px; }
.cs-hero-meta .cell .v { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(15px, 1.15vw, 19px); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
.cs-hero-meta .cell .v .bl { color: #dc2626; }
.cs-hero-meta .cell .v .gr { color: var(--green); }
@media (max-width: 720px) { .cs-hero-meta { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }

.cs-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 240px 1fr; gap: 48px; padding: 56px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.cs-section:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }
.cs-section .lab-col { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: #dc2626; text-transform: uppercase; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
.cs-section .lab-col .num { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 10px; }
.cs-section .body-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; max-width: 70ch; }
.cs-section .body-col h2 { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(24px, 2.4vw, 36px); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.15; }
.cs-section .body-col p { font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(15px, 1.1vw, 18px); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
.cs-section .body-col p strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
.cs-section .body-col p code { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--green); background: var(--bg-tertiary); padding: 1px 6px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
.cs-section .body-col ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin-top: 4px; }
.cs-section .body-col ul li { padding-left: 20px; position: relative; font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(14.5px, 1.05vw, 17px); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
.cs-section .body-col ul li::before { content: '+'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: #dc2626; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-weight: 600; }
.cs-section .body-col ul li strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
@media (max-width: 900px) { .cs-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; padding: 40px 0; } .cs-section .lab-col { flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: 12px; } }

.impact-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin-top: 8px; }
.impact-card { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 22px 24px; position: relative; }
.impact-card::before { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 2px; background: #dc2626; opacity: 0.85; }
.impact-card .k { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: #dc2626; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.impact-card .v { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(26px, 2.4vw, 38px); font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.impact-card .desc { font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
@media (max-width: 900px) { .impact-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
@media (max-width: 560px) { .impact-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

.cs-proof { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin-top: 20px; }
.cs-proof figure { margin: 0; background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); }
.cs-proof figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.cs-proof figcaption { padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
.cs-proof figcaption .t { display: block; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #dc2626; margin-bottom: 4px; }
@media (max-width: 700px) { .cs-proof { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

.cs-shots { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; margin-top: 20px; }
.cs-shots figure { margin: 0; background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); }
.cs-shots figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.cs-shots figcaption { padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }
.cs-shots figcaption .t { display: block; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #dc2626; margin-bottom: 4px; }

.stack-flat { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 8px; }
.stack-flat .chip { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 6px 12px; background: var(--bg-tertiary); border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--text-secondary); }
.stack-flat .chip.daily { border-color: #dc2626; color: #dc2626; }

.timeline-rail { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 0; margin-top: 8px; }
.timeline-rail .step { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr; gap: 22px; padding: 18px 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); align-items: baseline; }
.timeline-rail .step:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.timeline-rail .step .when { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: #dc2626; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 600; }
.timeline-rail .step .what { font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.55; }
.timeline-rail .step .what strong { color: var(--text-primary); }

.final-cta { background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg-card) 0%, var(--bg-tertiary) 100%); border: 1px solid #dc2626; padding: 48px 40px; margin-top: 48px; text-align: center; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
.final-cta::before { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.08) 0%, transparent 60%); pointer-events: none; }
.final-cta > * { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
.final-cta h2 { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 36px); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.15; }
.final-cta h2 .acc { color: #dc2626; }
.final-cta p { font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 17px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 24px; max-width: 580px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }

.confidential { padding: 16px 20px; background: var(--bg-tertiary); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 2px solid var(--text-dim); margin-top: 28px; font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--text-dim); line-height: 1.55; }
.confidential strong { color: var(--text-secondary); font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; display: inline-block; margin-right: 6px; }

/* Client pull-quote */
.cs-pullquote { margin-top: 32px; padding: 26px 30px; background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 2px solid #dc2626; position: relative; }
